     "text": "Kirk Hall and Williams Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI had the pleasure of consulting with Tyler Mercer July 25, 2025. This was a follow-up visit prompted by an upper respiratory infection (URI). During our consultation, I reviewed ongoing medical conditions current treatment plans.\n\nFirstly, regarding Tyler's Multiple sclerosis, his condition remains controlled. His Expanded Disability Status Scale (EDSS) score is 4.5, indicating mild disability. He is currently on dimethyl fumarate 240 mg, which has been effective in managing his symptoms. There have been no recent exacerbations or significant changes in his neurological status.\n\nSecondly, Tyler’s osteopenia continues to be well-managed. He is taking alendronate 70 mg, a medication that has helped stabilize his bone density. His latest bone density scan, although not immediately available, has shown stable results thus far.\n\nOn examination, Tyler's vital signs were within normal limits with a blood pressure of 124/89 and a weight of 216 pounds. The remainder of his physical exam, including neurological and musculoskeletal assessments, was unremarkable aside from minor URI symptoms.\n\nSocially, Tyler disclosed that he uses vapes on weekends. He drinks approximately one alcoholic beverage per week. There have been no recent changes in his smoking or drinking habits.\n\nIn summary, Tyler’s Multiple sclerosis and osteopenia are both under good control with his current medications. There are no immediate concerns or recommendations beyond his established treatment regimen.\n\nThank you for referring Tyler for this consultation. Please feel free to reach out if there are any further questions or if additional follow-up is needed.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Mackenzie Jacobs \nFamily Medicine \nKirk Hall and Williams Medical\n"
